          'ROIC: Superior for businesses with operating leases, complex capital structures, or significant off-balance-sheet items. Requires adjustments (capitalizing leases, removing excess cash) but gives a cleaner picture of true economic returns for asset-light and mixed models.',
          'ROE: Useful for banks and financials where equity is the regulatory capital constraint. For non-financial companies, ROE can be inflated by financial leverage — a company borrowing heavily can show 25% ROE while earning only 8% on its underlying assets.',
          'Rule of thumb: use ROCE for comparing utilities, pipelines, and miners; use ROIC for consumer staples, tech, and industrials; use ROE for banks and insurers.'
