        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Price-to-Tangible Book Value (P/TBV) is to bank analysts what P/E is to growth investors — the primary valuation anchor. A P/TBV of 1.0x means you are paying exactly what the hard assets are worth on the books. Above 1.0x means the market is paying a premium for franchise value, earnings power, or a superior management team. Below 1.0x raises an immediate question: is the market seeing loan losses or asset write-downs that are not yet reflected in the reported book value, or is this a genuine value opportunity?'
