        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'If you wanted to buy an entire company outright — every share, every obligation — what would it actually cost you? The answer is Enterprise Value (EV), not market capitalization. Market cap tells you what the equity is worth on the stock market. Enterprise Value tells you the total price tag: you would pay market cap to buy the shares, assume all the company\'s debt (which you must now service), and receive all the company\'s cash (which reduces your net outlay). EV is the standard basis for comparing acquisition costs, and it underpins the most widely used valuation multiples: EV/EBITDA, EV/EBIT, and EV/Revenue.'
