        text: 'Other Comprehensive Income (OCI) is a catch-all for gains and losses that affect a company\'s equity but are deliberately excluded from net income under GAAP and IFRS. These items are considered either too volatile, too unrealised, or too long-cycle to reflect in a single period\'s earnings. Yet they are economically real — and for financial institutions, industrial companies with large pension plans, and multinationals with significant foreign operations, OCI can be larger in magnitude than reported net income in any given year.'
