        type: 'callout',
        variant: 'tip',
        title: 'Reconstructing the Direct Method from Disclosures',
        text: 'Even when a company uses the indirect method, you can approximate direct method figures. Cash collected from customers ≈ Revenue − Change in Accounts Receivable. Cash paid to suppliers ≈ COGS + Change in Inventory − Change in Accounts Payable. These reconstructions are imperfect but powerful for spotting revenue quality problems — if cash collected from customers is consistently well below reported revenue, aggressive revenue recognition may be at work.'
