        text: 'The Dividend Discount Model values a stock based on the present value of all its future dividend payments. The logic is straightforward: if you own a stock forever, the only cash you ever receive is dividends. Therefore, a stock is worth exactly the sum of all future dividends, discounted back to today. While this seems limited, it is the theoretically purest form of equity valuation.',
