        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Most valuation methods focus on future earnings power. Asset-based valuation takes a different approach: it estimates what the company\'s assets are worth in the hands of a buyer or in dissolution. This method is most relevant when a company\'s earnings power is low relative to its asset value, when the business is being wound down, or when asset markets are more liquid and transparent than the business\'s earnings (as in real estate or investment holding companies).',
