        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Liquidation analysis matters most for distressed companies and bankruptcy situations. Secured creditors receive proceeds from collateral first; unsecured creditors receive what remains; equity typically receives nothing in a liquidation. Estimating liquidation value requires applying haircuts to each asset class: cash (100%), receivables (70-90%), inventory (40-60%), real estate (80-100% in an orderly sale), and machinery (20-50% depending on specialty). Adding these up and subtracting liabilities gives the equity value in a liquidation scenario.',
