        text: 'Early-stage SaaS companies often report negative EBITDA because they are investing heavily in sales, marketing, and R&D to capture market share. Using EV/EBITDA for these companies either produces a meaningless negative multiple or forces analysts to use future-year estimates so far out that they become unreliable. EV/Gross Profit sidesteps this problem: gross profit is almost always positive even for early-stage SaaS, and it captures the "true" profitability of the subscription business before the discretionary growth investments.',
