        text: 'Turnaround investing involves buying companies experiencing significant operational, financial, or competitive distress on the thesis that the problems are temporary and fixable rather than permanent and structural. When the thesis is right, the returns can be extraordinary — distressed businesses often trade at fractions of their potential value. When the thesis is wrong, the losses can be severe. The critical skill is distinguishing between a company that stumbled and one that is terminally broken.',
