        variant: 'info',
        title: 'When to Use Sortino Over Sharpe',
        text: 'Sortino is particularly valuable for evaluating strategies with asymmetric return distributions — options strategies, managed futures, or any fund that actively targets downside protection. If a strategy has positive skew (frequent small losses but occasional very large gains), Sharpe underestimates it. If it has negative skew (frequent small gains but occasional catastrophic losses), Sharpe overestimates it. Sortino corrects both biases by focusing only on the harmful volatility.'
