        text: 'Financial myths are particularly dangerous because many of them feel correct. They align with intuition, get repeated constantly in casual conversation, and are sometimes superficially true in specific narrow circumstances. But at their core, they lead investors toward decisions that systematically undermine long-term returns. Here are ten of the most pervasive — and most costly — investing myths, with the evidence that debunks each one.',
