          'Myth: "A stock that has fallen a lot is a bargain." Reality: a stock down 70% can fall another 70%. Price decline creates the opportunity to ask whether the stock is now cheap relative to intrinsic value — but the decline itself says nothing about cheapness. Many stocks fall to zero.',
