          'Myth: "You can time the market with enough skill or information." Reality: professional fund managers with full-time research teams, superior data, and lower transaction costs fail to consistently outperform the market index. Over 80% underperform over 15-year periods. Individual investors outperforming on a consistent, statistically significant basis is extraordinarily rare.',
          'Myth: "Dividend stocks are safer than growth stocks." Reality: dividends are not free money — a stock\'s price drops by approximately the dividend amount on the ex-dividend date. Dividend stocks provide income but do not inherently provide more safety. Companies that cut dividends can fall sharply. High dividend yields can signal financial distress.',
          'Myth: "Bonds are risk-free." Reality: bonds carry interest rate risk (rising rates cause bond prices to fall), credit risk (the issuer may default), and inflation risk (the fixed payment buys less over time). The 2022 US bond market experienced its worst calendar year in modern history as rates rose sharply.',
