          'Market makers (specialists): each options exchange has designated market makers required to continuously quote bids and asks for all listed contracts. In exchange for this obligation, they receive advantages like reduced fees and preferential order flow.',
          'Payment for order flow in options: retail options orders are often sold by brokers to wholesalers (like Citadel Securities or Susquehanna) who execute them off-exchange at quoted prices. The debate about whether this helps or hurts retail options traders is ongoing.',
