        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'A traditional 60/40 portfolio might look balanced by dollars, but a portfolio analysis quickly reveals that equities — being far more volatile than bonds — contribute roughly 80–90% of total portfolio risk. Risk parity corrects this imbalance by sizing each asset class so that its contribution to overall portfolio volatility is equal, rather than its dollar weight. The result is a genuinely diversified portfolio across risk, not just across capital.',
