        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'In a risk parity portfolio, the marginal risk contribution of each asset equals every other asset\'s marginal risk contribution. Because bonds are far less volatile than equities, bonds receive much larger dollar allocations — often 3–5 times as much — to equalise their risk contribution. This typically requires leverage at the portfolio level to achieve a target overall volatility, which is one of the main practical challenges of risk parity implementation.',
