        text: 'The critical term is the last one: 2·w₁·w₂·σ₁·σ₂·ρ₁₂. When ρ = 1, this equals the maximum possible value and portfolio volatility equals the weighted average of individual volatilities — no diversification benefit. When ρ = 0, the cross term vanishes and portfolio volatility falls below the weighted average. When ρ = -1, the cross term is negative and in theory volatility can reach zero with the right weights.'
