        text: 'A football field chart is the standard way professional analysts communicate valuation uncertainty. Instead of presenting a single price target, the football field stacks horizontal bars — one for each valuation method — each showing a low-to-high range rather than a point estimate. The overlap zone across all methods becomes the analyst\'s highest-conviction fair value range. The name comes from the visual resemblance to a football field with yard lines across it.',
