        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Behavioral finance documents the systematic ways human psychology causes investors to make decisions that deviate from rationality. These biases are not random errors that cancel out — they are predictable patterns that reliably harm long-term returns. Recognizing them in your own thinking is the first step toward building a process that partially corrects for them.',
