        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Nassim Taleb coined the term "narrative fallacy" in The Black Swan to describe our compulsive need to weave events into coherent, causal stories. A sequence of events is difficult to hold in memory. A sequence of events connected by a cause-and-effect narrative is easy to remember, easy to repeat, and emotionally satisfying. The problem: the stories we construct are often incorrect, and in investing, acting on a compelling but incorrect story can be enormously costly.',
