        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'A currency swap involves exchanging principal and interest payments in one currency for principal and interest payments in another. Unlike interest rate swaps, principal is actually exchanged at the start and returned at maturity. A US company issuing euro-denominated bonds to access European investor demand might simultaneously enter a USD/EUR currency swap, converting its euro coupon obligations back into dollar payments. This eliminates foreign exchange exposure while still benefiting from the European bond market\'s pricing.',
