        text: 'Every trade has a cost beyond the commission. Two of the most significant — and most overlooked — are slippage and market impact. Slippage is the difference between the price you expected when you decided to trade and the price you actually received. Market impact is the price movement caused by your own order. For retail investors these costs are small; for institutions moving millions of shares, they can wipe out an entire alpha thesis.',
