        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'A liquid large-cap like Apple might trade with a $0.01 spread on a $180 stock — a negligible 0.006%. A small-cap stock might have a $0.20 spread on a $10 stock — a 2% round-trip cost before the market moves at all. This spread is earned by the market maker every time a retail investor hits the market order button.',
