        text: 'Paper trading (simulating trades with real-time prices but no real capital) is valuable not primarily for validating alpha — the sample period is usually too short for statistical significance — but for uncovering operational issues: data feed problems, order logic errors, rebalancing timing, and dividend handling. A strategy that breaks during paper trading would have broken with real money. Run at least 3-6 months of paper trading before going live.',
