        text: 'Monte Carlo simulation stress-tests how sensitive a strategy is to the specific order and magnitude of historical returns. It does NOT test: whether the underlying factor relationship will persist in the future, whether the strategy was overfit to historical data, or whether a genuinely new market environment (unprecedented interest rates, new market structure, different regulatory framework) will emerge. A strategy can look robust to Monte Carlo simulation and still fail live because the factor it exploits decays or a genuinely novel regime arrives that is not represented in the historical data.',
