          'The cost: In a normal volatility environment (VIX 15-20), a 3-month 20% OTM put on the S&P 500 might cost 0.5-1.0% of notional. Annualised, that is 2-4% of portfolio value — a heavy drag if markets are flat or rising.',
          'Rolling puts: Most tail hedgers roll 3-month puts every quarter. In calm markets this produces a steady cost; in volatile markets the cost spikes because implied vol rises.',
