          'Threshold rebalancing (tolerance band): Rebalance only when an asset class drifts more than a set percentage from its target (e.g., ±5% band). More tax-efficient because it only triggers trades when drift is meaningful. The trade-off is that monitoring is ongoing rather than calendar-based.',
