        type: 'paragraph',
        text: 'Gross margin is the first profitability gate a business must pass through. Before a single dollar reaches operating income, revenue must first survive the cost of actually making or delivering the product. Gross margin tells you how much of each revenue dollar survives that first gauntlet — and its level sets a hard ceiling on everything below it: R&D spending, marketing, G&A, and ultimately net income. A business with a 20% gross margin can never generate a 25% operating margin, no matter how lean its overhead.'
